    "result_text": "All 56 tests pass with a clean build. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature on the `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}` endpoint. The request may now include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the response exposes a derived `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nFollowing the codebase's established pattern (derived read-only fields are `@Transient` getters on the `Owner` entity, auto-mapped to the generated DTO by MapStruct):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` field with getter/setter, plus a `@Transient getSalutation()` that composes the salutation exactly as specified.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` to the `OwnerFields` input schema and `salutation` as a `readOnly` field on the `Owner` output schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` carry both fields. MapStruct maps `title` in (via `toOwner`) and `title`/`salutation` out (via `toOwnerDto`) by name \u2014 no explicit `@Mapping` needed, consistent with the other derived fields.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table so the title survives to the subsequent GET. Tests run against the `hsqldb` profile.\n\nThe new `Cp45Tests.coreComposesSalutation` passes (`title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 `\"DR who\"`), and the full suite (56 tests) is green.",
